====================================================================================================
E2  Is alpha (content-vs-structure trust) a faithful explanation? (block interventions, nodes with content)
====================================================================================================
Intervention: zero the content block / zero the structure block of the fused feature, recompute memberships with the
fitted centers. delta = TV shift(content removed) - TV shift(structure removed). A faithful alpha gives
Spearman(alpha, delta) > 0 and higher content-flip rate in the high-alpha tercile. 'posthoc' = label-free margin
attribution (block contribution to d2(2nd)-d2(top)); 'normshare' = content share of the squared feature norm.

